% Test cases for the cervical traction policy (cervical_traction.le):
% synthetic claims, one per criterion of LCD L33823 and per device the LCD
% denies. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a medical
% reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. A cervical traction device is a purchase: no rental month.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base cervical_traction cases includes these resources:
    cervical_traction.

the knowledge base cervical_traction cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for an over-the-door device (E0860): the finding, the
% demonstration and the tolerance, the standard written order communicated
% before the date of service, the delivery and its proof.
scenario over_the_door_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the traction device.
    the HCPCS code of the traction device is "E0860".
    the traction device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy at C6 with arm pain".
    the appropriate use of the traction device was demonstrated to Ann.
    Ann tolerated the traction device.
    the order for the traction device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the traction device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the traction device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the traction device includes order date.
    the order for the traction device includes description of the item.
    the order for the traction device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the traction device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the traction device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the traction device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the traction device.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Criterion 1 fails: the medical reviewer finds no impairment requiring
% traction.
scenario no_impairment is:
    claim 1 is for the traction device.
    the HCPCS code of the traction device is "E0860".
    the traction device is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Ben is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record documents tension headaches and no musculoskeletal or neurologic impairment of the cervical spine".
    the appropriate use of the traction device was demonstrated to Ben.
    Ben tolerated the traction device.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Criterion 2 fails: the record does not say the beneficiary tolerated the
% device.
scenario not_tolerated is:
    claim 1 is for the traction device.
    the HCPCS code of the traction device is "E0860".
    the traction device is furnished to Cy.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical spondylosis with radiculopathy".
    the appropriate use of the traction device was demonstrated to Cy.
    rn expects answers [].

% A pneumatic frame device (E0849) by criterion A (a treated TMJ
% dysfunction), and one by criterion C (25 pounds of traction ordered).
scenario higher_force_by_record is:
    claim 1 is for the frame device.
    the HCPCS code of the frame device is "E0849".
    the frame device is furnished to Dee.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy".
    the appropriate use of the frame device was demonstrated to Dee.
    Dee tolerated the frame device.
    the medical record of Dee documents temporomandibular joint dysfunction.
    Dee has received treatment for the temporomandibular joint condition.
    claim 2 is for the second frame device.
    the HCPCS code of the second frame device is "E0855".
    the second frame device is furnished to Eve.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy".
    the appropriate use of the second frame device was demonstrated to Eve.
    Eve tolerated the second frame device.
    the treating practitioner orders or documents the medical necessity for 25 pounds of cervical traction in the home.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% An E0855 device with 15 pounds ordered and no TMJ: the record states no
% additional criterion, so the answer is conditional on the chin halter
% finding (criterion B).
scenario higher_force_not_decided is:
    claim 1 is for the frame device.
    the HCPCS code of the frame device is "E0855".
    the frame device is furnished to Fay.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy".
    the appropriate use of the frame device was demonstrated to Fay.
    Fay tolerated the frame device.
    the treating practitioner orders or documents the medical necessity for 15 pounds of cervical traction in the home.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding chin halter unusable about Fay is established"].

% The Council finds the record shows no distortion of the jaw or neck
% anatomy: criterion B unsupported, and neither A nor C stated.
scenario chin_halter_council is:
    claim 1 is for the frame device.
    the HCPCS code of the frame device is "E0849".
    the frame device is furnished to Gus.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy".
    the appropriate use of the frame device was demonstrated to Gus.
    Gus tolerated the frame device.
    the finding chin halter unusable about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record documents no surgery or deformity of the jaw or neck; the practitioner's note cites the beneficiary's preference for the pneumatic device".
    rn expects answers [].

% A headboard device (E0840) and an ambulatory device (E0856): never
% reasonable and necessary.
scenario denied_devices is:
    claim 1 is for the headboard device.
    the HCPCS code of the headboard device is "E0840".
    the headboard device is furnished to Hal.
    the residence of Hal is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the appropriate use of the headboard device was demonstrated to Hal.
    Hal tolerated the headboard device.
    claim 2 is for the ambulatory device.
    the HCPCS code of the ambulatory device is "E0856".
    the ambulatory device is furnished to Hal.
    the appropriate use of the ambulatory device was demonstrated to Hal.
    Hal tolerated the ambulatory device.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the traction device.
    the HCPCS code of the traction device is "E0860".
    the traction device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding impairment requiring cervical traction about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cervical radiculopathy at C6 with arm pain".
    the appropriate use of the traction device was demonstrated to Ann.
    Ann tolerated the traction device.
    the order for the traction device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the traction device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the traction device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the traction device includes order date.
    the order for the traction device includes description of the item.
    the order for the traction device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the traction device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the traction device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the traction device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the traction device"]].
